  "type": "numerical",
  "level": 2,
  "question": {
    "text": "A travelling microscope is used to determine the refractive index of a glass slab. If 40 divisions are there in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math> on main scale and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>50</mn></math> Vernier scale divisions are equal to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>49</mn></math> main scale divisions, then least count of the travelling microscope is _____&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math>.",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "5",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Given here, main scale reading,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>M</mi><mi>S</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>40</mn></mfrac><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math></p><p>And,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>50</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mi>V</mi><mi>S</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>49</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mi>M</mi><mi>S</mi></math></p><p>Least count of travelling microscope is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>L</mi><mi>C</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>M</mi><mi>S</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>V</mi><mi>S</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mi>M</mi><mi>S</mi><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>49</mn><mn>50</mn></mfrac><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>M</mi><mi>S</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>50</mn></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><mi>M</mi><mi>S</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>50</mn></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>40</mn></mfrac><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2000</mn></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math></p>",
